    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0416" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 PW/9–1145: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-11">September 11,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received September 18—6 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–1067. American Interests—Japan. Foreign Office note, September 7, states Swiss
                    Minister Tokyo had lengthy discussion with Japanese Foreign Office with regard
                    contents Department’s 1992, June 8.<anchor n="48" xml:id="d271-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Swiss Minister states it would seem that Japanese authorities made every effort
                    to give proper food to internees Shanghai region despite considerable
                    difficulties they encountered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
